      {
        "text": "Abdelnasser Rashid has been the 21st District's State Representative since January 2023. Previously, he was a deputy chief of staff to Cook County Clerk David Orr. He passed a bill to ban PFAS in consumer products. He passed another bill creating a committee to address PFAS in wastewater. He passed legislation prohibiting community colleges from using artificial intelligence as the sole source of instruction. He passed a bill requiring state guidance on expanding dual language programs. He proposed a bill limiting rent increases at mobile home parks to 3% annually. He introduced a constitutional amendment to allow graduated income tax rates. He sponsored a bill to repeal a state law penalizing companies that boycott Israel.",
